Trap is a physical and systemic object.
Trap can be set or sprung.
State sprung is initial.
Base is a physical and systemic object.
Jaw is a physical and systemic object.
Jaw can be held back or released.
Transverse Spring is a physical and systemic object.
Transverse Spring can be tensioned or relaxed.
Arm is a physical and systemic object.
Inward Extension is a physical and systemic object.
Perforated Ears is a physical and systemic object.
Locking Bar is a physical and systemic object.
Locking Bar can be engaged or disengaged.
Trigger is a physical and systemic object.
Trigger can be at rest or pressed.
State at rest is initial.
Pintle is a physical and systemic object.
Staple Pintle is a physical and systemic object.
Shank Pintle is a physical and systemic object.
Catch is a physical and systemic object.
Catch can be engaged or released.
Front End is a physical and systemic object.
Shoulder is a physical and systemic object.
Pintle-Eye is a physical and systemic object.
Securing-Plates is a physical and systemic object.
Base Staple is a physical and systemic object.
Rear Eye is a physical and systemic object.
Shank is a physical and systemic object.
Material is a physical and systemic object.
Shape is an informatical and systemic object.
Animal is a physical and environmental object.
Animal can be free or caught.
State free is initial.
State caught is final.
Operator is a physical and environmental object.
Setting is an informatical and systemic process.
Springing is an informatical and systemic process.
Pressing is an informatical and systemic process.
Releasing is an informatical and systemic process.
Disengaging is an informatical and systemic process.
Forcing is an informatical and systemic process.
Catching is an informatical and systemic process.
Trap consists of Base, Jaw, Transverse Spring, Arm, Inward Extension, Perforated Ears, Locking Bar, Trigger, and Pintle.
Jaw consists of Front End.
Perforated Ears consists of Shank.
Locking Bar consists of Rear Eye.
Trigger consists of Catch.
Catch consists of Shoulder, Pintle-Eye, and Securing-Plates.
Base consists of Base Staple.
Staple Pintle is a Pintle.
Shank Pintle is a Pintle.
Base exhibits Material.
Front End exhibits Shape.
Operator handles Setting.
Setting requires Locking Bar.
Setting requires Catch.
Setting changes Trap from sprung to set.
Animal handles Springing.
Springing changes Trap from set to sprung.
Springing changes Animal from free to caught.
Springing invokes Pressing.
Springing invokes Releasing.
Springing invokes Disengaging.
Springing invokes Forcing.
Springing invokes Catching.
Animal handles Pressing.
Pressing changes Trigger from at rest to pressed.
Releasing requires Trigger at state pressed.
Releasing changes Catch from engaged to released.
Disengaging requires Catch at state released.
Disengaging changes Locking Bar from engaged to disengaged.
Forcing requires Locking Bar at state disengaged.
Forcing requires Transverse Spring.
Forcing changes Transverse Spring from tensioned to relaxed.
Forcing changes Jaw from held back to released.
Catching requires Jaw at state released.
Catching requires Front End.
Catching changes Animal from free to caught.
